---
// Article body from Figma nodes 14543:882 and 14543:900 — an 808px reading column
// holding an intro, four "Challenge N" sections and a closing paragraph, with a
// full-width image between the second and third.
//
// Two inconsistencies in the source were normalised rather than reproduced: the
// intro paragraphs mixed Inter and Geist between sections, and Challenge 4's
// bullet copy was hard-set to #2c2a2a while the others inherited the body colour.
// Everything here is Inter with the inherited 70%-opacity body colour.
//
// Figma spacing: 48px between sections, 32px within a section, 16px between a
// heading and its paragraph, 88px before the image and 80px after it.
const sections = [
  {
    heading: 'Challenge 1: Information Overload and Passive Consumption',
    intro:
      'With an endless stream of tutorials, courses, and documentation available, it is easy to fall into the trap of passive reading or video watching without actually retaining actionable knowledge.',
    bullets: [
      {
        lead: 'Practice Active Recall:',
        text: ' Instead of re-reading notes or re-watching videos, test yourself on key concepts immediately after reviewing them.',
      },
      {
        lead: 'Build While Learning:',
        text: ' Apply new concepts directly to small, practical projects rather than relying solely on structured tutorials.',
      },
      {
        lead: 'Curate Your Inputs:',
        text: ' Filter out low-value content and focus on high-signal resources to protect your cognitive bandwidth.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Challenge 2: Inconsistent Habit Formation',
    intro:
      'Starting a new learning path with high enthusiasm often leads to burnout when routine daily tasks, fatigue, or competing priorities interfere with your momentum.',
    bullets: [
      {
        lead: 'Set Micro-Goals:',
        text: ' Break complex subjects into bite-sized, 15-minute daily sessions to maintain steady consistency without feeling overwhelmed.',
      },
      {
        lead: 'Track Streaks and Milestones:',
        text: ' Use visual habit trackers or learning logs to reinforce momentum and hold yourself accountable.',
      },
      {
        lead: 'Time-Block Focused Work:',
        text: ' Schedule dedicated, distraction-free focus blocks in your primary calendar for deliberate practice.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Challenge 3: Transitioning from Theory to Execution',
    intro:
      'Understanding a concept in isolation does not automatically mean you can apply it to solve complex, real-world problems with real constraints.',
    bullets: [
      {
        lead: 'Embrace Project-Based Iteration:',
        text: ' Build functional prototypes, gather user or peer feedback, and refine your work based on practical constraints.',
      },
      {
        lead: 'Reverse-Engineer Real Examples:',
        text: ' Deconstruct successful products, systems, or case studies to understand the underlying decisions and trade-offs.',
      },
      {
        lead: 'Seek Early Feedback:',
        text: ' Share work-in-progress with peers or mentors to identify blind spots early in your development process.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Challenge 4: Overcoming Skill Plateaus',
    intro:
      'As initial quick wins diminish, tackling advanced concepts often leads to friction, self-doubt, and temporary stagnation.',
    bullets: [
      {
        lead: 'Focus on Problem-Solving Over Completion:',
        text: ' Frame your learning around solving specific problems rather than simply finishing a curriculum.',
      },
      {
        lead: 'Prioritize First Principles:',
        text: ' Shift focus from memorizing tools or frameworks to mastering foundational principles that do not change over time.',
      },
      {
        lead: 'Share Your Process:',
        text: ' Document and share your progress publicly or with a community to build accountability and gain fresh perspectives.',
      },
    ],
  },
];

const beforeImage = sections.slice(0, 2);
const afterImage = sections.slice(2);

const bodyText = 'text-[17px] leading-[1.8] opacity-70 sm:text-[20px]';
const sectionHeading =
  'text-[26px] font-medium leading-[1.3] tracking-[-1px] sm:text-[32px] sm:tracking-[-1.5px]';
const subHeading = 'font-geist text-[20px] font-medium leading-[1.4] tracking-[-0.8px] sm:text-[24px]';
const bulletList = 'flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 ps-[30px] text-[17px] leading-[1.7] sm:text-[20px]';
---

<div class="relative z-10 mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-[808px] px-4 text-white light:text-[#030003]">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-12">
    <div class={`flex flex-col gap-[1.8em] ${bodyText}`}>
      <p>
        In today’s fast-moving environment, acquiring new skills isn't just about logging hours; it is
        about optimizing how you absorb, retain, and apply knowledge. Whether you are mastering product
        design, software engineering, or strategic decision-making, learning efficiently dictates how
        quickly you can turn ideas into real-world results.
      </p>
      <p>
        Here are four common challenges learners face, along with practical strategies to overcome them
        and build better outcomes.
      </p>
    </div>

    {
      beforeImage.map((section) => (
        <section class="flex flex-col gap-8">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
            <h2 class={sectionHeading}>{section.heading}</h2>
            <p class={bodyText}>{section.intro}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
            <h3 class={subHeading}>Overcoming the challenge:</h3>
            <ul class={bulletList}>
              {section.bullets.map((bullet) => (
                <li class="opacity-70">
                  <strong class="font-semibold tracking-[-0.2px]">{bullet.lead}</strong>
                  {bullet.text}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <img
    src="/images/post-inline-1.png"
    alt=""
    width="1212"
    height="717"
    class="mt-[88px] aspect-[808/478] w-full rounded-[24px] object-cover"
    loading="lazy"
    decoding="async"
  />

  <div class="mt-20 flex flex-col gap-12">
    {
      afterImage.map((section) => (
        <section class="flex flex-col gap-8">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
            <h2 class={sectionHeading}>{section.heading}</h2>
            <p class={bodyText}>{section.intro}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
            <h3 class={subHeading}>Overcoming the challenge:</h3>
            <ul class={bulletList}>
              {section.bullets.map((bullet) => (
                <li class="opacity-70">
                  <strong class="font-semibold tracking-[-0.2px]">{bullet.lead}</strong>
                  {bullet.text}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <p class={bodyText}>
      By addressing these core challenges, you turn learning from a passive effort into a structured,
      repeatable engine for growth. Focus on execution, build consistently, and measure progress by the
      tangible value you create.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
